WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.582
Hi, I'm Harrow!

00:00:02.582 --> 00:00:06.068
Here is how Mercury 3, a diffusion language model, writes a block

00:00:06.068 --> 00:00:07.230
of text at once.

00:00:09.892 --> 00:00:13.251
Instead of one token per pass, it drafts a whole block, then

00:00:13.251 --> 00:00:14.930
refines it over a few passes.

00:00:18.275 --> 00:00:21.835
The usual model writes one token per pass, and each pass streams

00:00:21.835 --> 00:00:23.022
every weight from memory.

00:00:23.782 --> 00:00:27.575
A diffusion model predicts every masked slot at once, so the same

00:00:27.575 --> 00:00:28.839
reads produce more text.

00:00:30.633 --> 00:00:32.742
The current block starts as all masks.

00:00:32.742 --> 00:00:36.356
The denoiser reads it, plus the prompt and finished blocks, which never

00:00:36.356 --> 00:00:37.862
change and can be cached.

00:00:38.282 --> 00:00:41.700
In one pass it guesses every masked slot, and keeps only

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:42.943
the most confident guesses.

00:00:43.363 --> 00:00:47.219
The rest go back to masks for another pass, with more neighbours now fixed.

00:00:47.639 --> 00:00:50.876
When the block is full, it streams out, becomes context, and

00:00:50.876 --> 00:00:52.053
the next block begins.

00:00:53.817 --> 00:00:55.213
Fewer passes is not free.

00:00:56.406 --> 00:00:58.969
Fixing more tokens per pass means fewer passes.

00:00:59.389 --> 00:01:02.435
But each slot is sampled on its own, so hot dog and

00:01:02.435 --> 00:01:03.958
ice cream can become hot cream.

00:01:04.378 --> 00:01:08.206
And fewer passes only become speed with an engine built for it,

00:01:08.206 --> 00:01:09.481
which Inception keeps private.

00:01:11.175 --> 00:01:15.421
Inception's chart starts at Mercury One Mini, whose size it has never published.

00:01:15.841 --> 00:01:20.641
Mercury 3 sits about forty times larger, at about three times the quality average.

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:25.440
On OpenRouter, Mercury 3 is the fastest of the three.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.507
But the launch chart's one thousand sixty-eight becomes three hundred and two.

00:01:30.975 --> 00:01:33.074
The parallel draft is real speed.

00:01:33.074 --> 00:01:36.923
The launch number is Inception's own, and routed traffic keeps less.

00:01:39.358 --> 00:01:43.052
Draft a block, refine it in parallel, cache what is finished, and

00:01:43.052 --> 00:01:45.207
check speed claims where real traffic runs.

00:01:45.626 --> 00:01:47.639
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:47.639 --> 00:01:48.214
I'm Harrow.

00:01:48.214 --> 00:01:48.502
Bye!
